  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116316",
      "title": "Configuring Http Requests",
      "lectureOrder": 225,
      "videoOrder": 214,
      "sourceHash": "b032fb8201e0cf896f874dc9eca593a8e5dd45727795e57cf74d251735effac4",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.57,
          "end": 3.3,
          "en": "Now, before we'll output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.3,
          "end": 6.18,
          "en": "this response data in the UI,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.18,
          "end": 9.57,
          "en": "I first of all wanna briefly show you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.57,
          "end": 12.87,
          "en": "that you could also configure this request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.87,
          "end": 14.94,
          "en": "by passing a second argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.94,
          "end": 18.03,
          "en": "a configuration object to this get method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.03,
          "end": 21.72,
          "en": "such that this next function is triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.72,
          "end": 25.233,
          "en": "with different data than the response data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.43,
          "end": 30.33,
          "en": "You can configure this by setting the observe setting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.33,
          "end": 33.24,
          "en": "on this configuration object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.24,
          "end": 37.29,
          "en": "And you can, for example, set this to response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.29,
          "end": 39.81,
          "en": "even though my IDE does not give me that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.81,
          "end": 41.22,
          "en": "as a suggestion here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.22,
          "end": 44.433,
          "en": "but response is one of the allowed values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.69,
          "end": 48.51,
          "en": "If you do set this to response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.51,
          "end": 51.39,
          "en": "Angular will trigger this next function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.39,
          "end": 53.46,
          "en": "not with the response data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.46,
          "end": 57.32,
          "en": "but instead with the full response object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.32,
          "end": 61.143,
          "en": "So response is a more fitting name for this parameter then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.61,
          "end": 66.93,
          "en": "Now this response object still has a body property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.93,
          "end": 69.96000000000001,
          "en": "which actually contains the response data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.96000000000001,
          "end": 73.47,
          "en": "but this may now actually be null,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 73.47,
          "end": 75.93,
          "en": "simply because theoretically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.93,
          "end": 79.53,
          "en": "the response could of course not contain any body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.53,
          "end": 82.8,
          "en": "That's why we need to add this question mark here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.8,
          "end": 86.31,
          "en": "to access this places property conditionally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.31,
          "end": 89.55,
          "en": "only if body is not null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.55,
          "end": 91.68,
          "en": "So we can of course, also lock this entire",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.68,
          "end": 93.24000000000001,
          "en": "response object here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.24000000000001,
          "end": 96.72,
          "en": "And if I do so, and I then reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.72,
          "end": 99.06,
          "en": "you'll see that after a short while,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.06,
          "end": 102.99000000000001,
          "en": "this HttpResponse object is being locked here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.99000000000001,
          "end": 106.47,
          "en": "And that's an object that contains the body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.47,
          "end": 109.92,
          "en": "the parsed body to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.92,
          "end": 113.22,
          "en": "but also headers, the information,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.22,
          "end": 115.47,
          "en": "whether it's a success response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.47,
          "end": 120.283,
          "en": "the exact status code and status text, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.44,
          "end": 124.02,
          "en": "Now, besides observing the response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.02,
          "end": 128.13,
          "en": "you could also observe events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.13,
          "end": 130.83,
          "en": "That's another supported setting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.83,
          "end": 132.48,
          "en": "And if you do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.48,
          "end": 136.41,
          "en": "the next function will actually get triggered multiple times",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 136.41,
          "end": 140.61,
          "en": "instead of just once, as it was previously the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.61,
          "end": 144.21,
          "en": "Because it will now get triggered for different events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 144.21,
          "end": 148.053,
          "en": "that occur during that request response lifecycle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 149.04,
          "end": 153.84,
          "en": "So here, I'll log that event so that we get an idea for",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 153.84,
          "end": 155.55,
          "en": "how often it is being triggered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 155.55,
          "end": 159.15,
          "en": "And if I save that and I reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 159.15,
          "end": 161.975,
          "en": "you will see that we got one log right at the start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 161.975,
          "end": 165.66,
          "en": "and then at some point, also the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 165.66,
          "end": 167.67000000000002,
          "en": "So I got two logs here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 167.67000000000002,
          "end": 170.88,
          "en": "Now, the first event is super simple, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.88,
          "end": 174.582,
          "en": "that in the end is simply an event that's being emitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.582,
          "end": 178.5,
          "en": "to tell us that the request was sent, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 178.5,
          "end": 181.173,
          "en": "And then some point, we got the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 182.01,
          "end": 184.14,
          "en": "But still, this now shows us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.14,
          "end": 187.26,
          "en": "that the next function is triggered multiple times,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 187.26,
          "end": 188.61,
          "en": "not just once.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 188.61,
          "end": 191.88,
          "en": "And if you're interested in performing different actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 191.88,
          "end": 193.53,
          "en": "at different points of time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 193.53,
          "end": 196.53,
          "en": "during that request response life cycle,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 196.53,
          "end": 199.203,
          "en": "observing the events might be what you want to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 200.28,
          "end": 202.59,
          "en": "Now here, I'll get rid of that though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 202.59,
          "end": 207.3,
          "en": "and I'll go back to working with just the response data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 207.3,
          "end": 208.74,
          "en": "as we did before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 208.74,
          "end": 210.18,
          "en": "but it's of course worth knowing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 210.18,
          "end": 212.43,
          "en": "about these alternative options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 212.43,
          "end": 215.04,
          "en": "But with that, we can now finally make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 215.04,
          "end": 217.983,
          "en": "that these places are also shown on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
